    "updated_at": "2022-09-29T23:31:45Z",
    "body": "I found when Blink changed: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/a736194f01cfbb2688134cdfdf66f85996719ee4\r\n\r\n> We had 10,000 limit only when we add OPTIONs via IDL features, and no limit for OPTIONs added by the HTML parser.  We observed 40,000+ OPTIONs were practically used, and the 10,000 limit didn't make sense.\r\n\r\nI guess the point is it'd be weird if you had `<select>... 50_000 options ...</select>` via the parser, and then did `select.options.length++`, that would truncate you down to 10_000 options. Hmm....",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
